      "title": "Transposing Melodies by Interval",
      "level": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "**Track:** transposition | **Difficulty:** 3/10 | **Time:** ~8 min"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Move every note by the same interval — up a tone from D to E major, down a fourth from G to D."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scale-degree-method",
      "title": "Scale-degree method",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "If a phrase starts on the 5th of G (D), the same phrase in D major starts on A (5th of D). Faster than note-by-note for experienced players."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "accidentals",
      "title": "Accidentals",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Move accidentals with their notes. C♮ in F major becomes D♮ when transposing up a whole step to G — not C♯ unless harmony demands it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
